<title>THAILAND: Thai sugar vessel movements on March 12.</title>
<headline>Thai sugar vessel movements on March 12.</headline>
<dateline>BANGKOK 1997-03-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Independent surveyors detailed Thai sugar freight movement as follows (in tonne tel quels):</p>
<p>Vessel		  Position	  Quantity    Destination</p>
<p>Great Universe	SLD Mar 04	14,300	Indonesia</p>
<p>Feng Zhan	     SLD Mar 08	12,000	Indonesia</p>
<p>Golden Glint	  SLD Mar 08	 6,300	Indonesia</p>
<p>Myohyang 3	    SLD Mar 10	13,900	Indonesia</p>
<p>Nocholas I.K.	 SLD Mar 07	15,000	S.Korea</p>
<p>Tropical Damsel     SLD Mar 03	 8,000	Japan</p>
<p>Delight		 SLD Mar 04	 5,850	Indonesia</p>
<p>Marina Lauri	  SLD Mar 07	10,000	China</p>
<p>Han Chaun	     SLD Mar 08	12,000	Indonesia</p>
<p>Kum Gang		SLD Mar 06	12,000	Indonesia</p>
<p>Cheugnson	     SLD Mar 07	14,700	S.Korea</p>
<p>Ais Mamas	     SLD Mar 04	14,000	S.Korea</p>
<p>Orient Express	SLD Mar 09	   700	Indonesia</p>
<p>Pitak Samut	   SLD Mar 06	12,000	Japan</p>
<p>Guang Fu Quan	 SLD Mar 10	14,700	S.Korea</p>
<p>Ya Jiang		SLD Mar 07	 4,500	Indonesia</p>
<p>Sangthai Quartz     SLD Mar 09	 1,300	Singapore</p>
<p>Tropic Confidence   SLD Mar 10	14,700	S.Korea</p>
<p>Huang Hua	     ETD Mar 14-15   14,000	S.Korea</p>
<p>Feng Tao		ETD Mar 13	13,000	Indonesia</p>
<p>Progress Excellence ETD Mar 16	13,200	Indonesia</p>
<p>Lisson Leader	 ETD Mar 11	14,000	S.Korea</p>
<p>Hyoksin		 ETD Mar 17	13,200	Indonesia</p>
<p>Chong Chon Gang     ETD Mar 17	12,000	Indonesia</p>
<p>Tong Chuan	    ETD Mar 16	12,000	China</p>
<p>Alam Teladan	  ETD Mar 11	16,800	Malaysia</p>
<p>Kapitan Lyubchenko  ETD Mar 16	12,000	Indonesia</p>
<p>Kapitan Samoylenko  ETD Mar 14	12,000	Russia</p>
<p>Great Best 1	  ETD Mar 20	13,000	Indonesia</p>
<p>NOTE: SLD indicates that the vessel has left, ETA = Estimated Time of Arrival, ETD = Estimated Time of Departure,</p>
<p>ETR = Estimated Time of Readiness, L/CAN indicated period when vessels are expected in for loading or be cancelled.</p>
</text>
